<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <IsTestProject>true</IsTestProject>
    <IsPackable>false</IsPackable>

    <!--
    xUnit v4 generates its own entry point, so the test project is an executable and is run with the
    dotnet run command given in the README, not with `dotnet test`.

    `dotnet test` reports "Zero tests ran" here and exits 5. That is not a symptom of anything being
    wrong with the tests: running the test executable directly finds and passes all of them. The
    cause is that `dotnet test` reaches xUnit's in-process console runner rather than its
    Microsoft.Testing.Platform runner, and the two do not share a protocol on this SDK.

    The obvious fixes were tried and are recorded so nobody repeats them. Setting
    TestingPlatformDotnetTestSupport on this project changes the error but still reports zero tests.
    Adding a "test" section to global.json to select the Testing.Platform runner does not help either.
    Keeping xunit.runner.visualstudio alongside xunit.v3 does not help, and is the wrong execution
    model regardless, so it is deliberately absent.

    Revisit when the SDK or xUnit ships a combination that works. Until then the README's command is
    the supported one and CI uses it.
    -->
    <OutputType>Exe</OutputType>

    <!--
    No UseWPF, deliberately.

    The test project tests logic, not markup. Leaving WPF out keeps the test host free of a UI
    dispatcher, so tests stay fast and, more usefully, cannot accidentally depend on a running
    Application. Anything that genuinely needs a window or an XamlRoot cannot be unit tested, and
    pretending otherwise is how a suite ends up quietly asserting nothing.
    -->
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <!--
    Pinned to a version that exists. An earlier draft asked for xunit.v3 3.1.5, which was never
    published; NuGet resolved upward and reported NU1601. Harmless in itself, but a floor loose enough
    to resolve to something other than what was asked for is exactly how a build stops being
    reproducible.
    -->
    <PackageReference Include="xunit.v3" Version="4.0.1" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\src\KronosReborn.Core\KronosReborn.Core.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
